[32.522258, "o", "1\tST-101\tright_of_first_refusal\tagreed by the father\tOI-202\tMr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\n2\tST-102\tchildren_named\tboth children, with their ages\tOI-203\tThis concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\n3\tST-103\tovernight_stays\tseveral occasions at her home or with a sitter\tOI-204\tOn several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\n4\tST-104\taddressee\tthe father's attorney\tOI-201\tTo counsel for Mr Adler.\r\n5\tST-105\tinconsistent_accounts\twife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender\tOI-205\tMr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\n6\tST-106\tconcern\tviolation limb only\tOI-206\tI am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\n"]
[32.522676, "o", "7\tST-107\tbehavioural_plan\tthe stays have had no effect on the plan\tOI-207\tImogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\r\n8\tST-108\trequest\tno overnight stays in her care unless the father is present\tCL-302\tI ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\n9\tST-109\tenclosure\ta certified copy of the custodial plan\tOI-209\tA certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\n10\tST-110\ttone\tfirm and detailed\tOI-210\tI set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\n11\tST-111\tsender_signature\tthe sender's own name\tOI-211\tYours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\n12\tST-112\tsalutation\tDear Counsel\tCL-304\tDear Counsel,\r\n13\tST-113\tcopies\tcopied to the father\tCL-305\tCopy: Mr Adler.\r\n14\tST-114\treply_deadline\ta reply within seven days\tOI-299\tI would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\n"]
[32.522905, "o", "15\tST-115\tschool_reference\tthe school principal named\tOI-298\tThe school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\r\n16\tST-116\tmediation_offer\tan offer to mediate\tCL-399\tI remain open to mediation.\r\n17\tST-117\trequest\tno overnight stays unless father present\tOI-208\tI ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\n18\tST-118\tdelivery\tsent by email to counsel\tOI-299\tThe letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\n19\tST-119\ttone\tfirm and detailed\tOI-210\tThe position is set out firmly and in full detail below.\r\n20\tST-120\tmediation_terms\tmediation within 14 days\tCL-399\tI propose mediation within fourteen days of the date of this letter.\r\n21\tST-121\tdelivery\tsent by courier to counsel\tOI-299\tThe letter is to be delivered by courier to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\n"]
[32.523123, "o", "22\tST-122\tinconsistent_accounts\twife to the school only\tOI-205\tMr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\n23\tST-123\trequest\tno overnight unless father present\tCL-302\tNeither child should remain overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\n24\tST-124\tlegal_fees\tcosts to be borne by the father\tOI-299\tAll legal costs arising from this matter shall be borne by the father.\r\n25\tST-125\trequest\tno overnight stays unless father present\tOI-208\tNeither child is to stay overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\n26\tST-126\tenclosure\ta certified copy of the custodial plan\tOI-209\tA certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed with this letter.\r\n"]
[32.523544, "o", "27\tST-127\ttone\twarm and personal\tOI-210\tThe letter is written in a warm and personal tone, reflecting the ongoing relationship between the parents.\r\n28\tST-128\tcopies\tcopied to the children\tOI-299\tA copy of this letter has been provided to both children for their records.\r\n29\tST-129\taddressee\tthe father attorney\tOI-201\tThis letter is addressed to the attorney representing the father in this matter.\r\n"]
[32.523892, "o", "30\tST-130\tinconsistent_accounts\tbabysitter to me only\tOI-205\tMr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\n31\tST-131\tdelivery\tsent by hand delivery\tCL-306\tThe letter shall be sent by hand delivery to the office of opposing counsel.\r\n32\tST-132\trequest\tno overnight unless accompanied by a parent\tCL-302\tNo child shall remain overnight in Ms Corwin care unless accompanied by a parent or legal guardian.\r\n33\tST-133\tright_of_first_refusal\tthe mother agreed\tOI-202\tMs Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\n34\tST-134\tenclosure\tan uncertified summary of the plan\tOI-209\tAn uncertified summary of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\n35\tST-135\tsalutation\tDear Mr Adler\tCL-304\tDear Mr Adler,\r\n36\tST-136\tinconsistent_accounts\tbabysitter to clinicians\tOI-205\tMr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to her clinicians.\r\n"]
[32.52414, "o", "37\tST-137\ttone\tfirm and at length\tCL-304\tSet out the position firmly and at length.\r\n38\tST-138\tconcern\tshe may not appreciate\tCL-305\tI am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\n39\tST-139\tbehavioural_plan\tconfidence and setback missing stability\tCL-302\tImogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence, and the stays have set back her progress.\r\n40\tST-140\tchildren_named\tboth children with ages\tCL-303\tThis concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\n41\tST-141\tovernight_stays\tone child on one occasion\tOI-204\tOn one occasion, Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\n42\tST-142\tright_of_first_refusal\tnot overnight with anyone but parents\tOI-202\tThe children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\n43\tST-143\taddressee\tthe father's attorney\tCL-301\tTo counsel for Mr Adler.\r\n44\tST-144\trequest\tno overnight unless the mother is present\tCL-302\tI ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unles"]
[32.524349, "o", "s Ms Corwin is present.\r\n45\tST-145\ttone\tfirm and detailed\tCL-304\tI set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\n46\tST-146\tconcern\tno concern about the stays\tOI-206\tI have no concern that Ms Corwin fails to appreciate the stays.\r\n47\tST-147\tdelivery\tsent by email\tCL-306\tThe letter shall be sent by email to counsel.\r\n48\tST-148\tchildren_named\tNoor only\tOI-203\tThis concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\n49\tST-149\tsalutation\tDear Sir or Madam\tCL-304\tDear Sir or Madam,\r\n50\tST-150\tbehavioural_plan\tstays improved the plan\tOI-207\tImogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence and stability, and the stays have improved her progress.\r\n51\tST-151\tcopies\tcopied to the school\tCL-305\tCopy: the school principal.\r\n52\tST-152\tovernight_stays\tnever overnight at her home\tOI-204\tNeither child has ever stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter.\r\n53\tST-153\trequest\tno overnight unless father present\tOI-208\tI ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\n54\tST-154\tenclosure\tcertifie"]
